<title>ESTONIA: BALTIC 30 INDEX DOWN 0.51 PCT TO 102.37.</title>
<headline>BALTIC 30 INDEX DOWN 0.51 PCT TO 102.37.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Baltic 30 index, the only pan-Baltic index compiled by the region's three leading business newspapers, fell by 0.51 percent to 102.37 on Monday, Estonian's Aripaev business newspaper said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The Baltic 30 index covers the 10 leading stocks from the three Baltic stock markets and is compiled by Aripaev, Lithuania's Verslo Zinios and Latvia's Dienas bizness.</p>
<p>The index was 100 on its launch date of May 19.</p>
<p>-- Tallinn newsroom, +372 6209 201, reuters@reuters</p>
